From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium meta-browser maintainers <meta-browser@lists.openembedded.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] network: avoid Clang crash in defaulted origin comparison

Clang 20 crashes while parsing the defaulted equality operator for
OriginWithPossibleWildcards when its mojom CSPSource member provides a
templated operator==. Implement the equality comparison explicitly; this
preserves the generated comparison semantics and avoids triggering the
frontend crash.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE-specific]
---
 services/network/public/cpp/permissions_policy/origin_with_possible_wildcards.cc | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/network/public/cpp/permissions_policy/origin_with_possible_wildcards.cc b/services/network/public/cpp/permissions_policy/origin_with_possible_wildcards.cc
--- a/services/network/public/cpp/permissions_policy/origin_with_possible_wildcards.cc
+++ b/services/network/public/cpp/permissions_policy/origin_with_possible_wildcards.cc
@@ -96,3 +96,5 @@
-bool operator==(const OriginWithPossibleWildcards& lhs,
-                const OriginWithPossibleWildcards& rhs) = default;
+bool operator==(const OriginWithPossibleWildcards& lhs,
+                const OriginWithPossibleWildcards& rhs) {
+  return lhs.csp_source == rhs.csp_source;
+}
